# Site checks

One file per site in `pkg/sites/`, registered in `init`. The file implements `Site` and contains that site's request and response mapping. Nothing else imports a concrete site type.

```go
func init() { Register(&github{}) }

func (github) Method() string { return "register" } // register | login | password_reset
```

Map responses explicitly:

```go
// 429 or a known block page
return checker.Result{Status: checker.StatusRateLimited}

// email is registered
return checker.Result{Status: checker.StatusFound, Evidence: "Signup endpoint said this email is already registered.", DeleteURL: "...", SecurityURL: "..."}
```

Each site needs `testdata/<name>/found.http`, `not_found.http`, and `rate_limited.http`. `go test ./pkg/sites/ -run <Name>` must pass offline. Live requests belong in the manual `live` job.

Set `DeleteURL` and `SecurityURL` when the site has those pages.
